        return new \MyService();
    }
);
```

The service is created the first time it is resolved, and the same instance is returned on subsequent retrievals [1]:

```php
$first  = $container->get('session');
$second = $container->get('session');
// $first and $second refer to the same instance
```

Alternatively, pass `true` as the third argument to `set()`:

```php
$container->set(
    'session',
    function () {
        return new \MyService();
    },
    true
);
```

If the service was not registered as shared, use `getShared()` to retrieve a shared instance [1]:

```php
$service = $container->getShared('session');
```

