Use the container’s `bind()` method:

```php
use Phalcon\Container\Container;

$container = new Container();

$container->bind(LoggerInterface::class, FileLogger::class);
```

When a service type-hints `LoggerInterface`, the container autowires `FileLogger` automatically:

```php
$container->set('mailer', Mailer::class);

$mailer = $container->get('mailer');
```

`bind()` accepts the interface name and concrete class name, and returns a `ServiceDefinition` for further configuration [1][2].

With `Phalcon\ADR\Application`, you can register the binding directly:

```php
$application = (new Application())
    ->bind(OrderRepositoryInterface::class, DbOrderRepository::class);
```

Type-hinted dependencies are then autowired [3].

