Use `Phalcon\Session\Adapter\Libmemcached` with a `Phalcon\Storage\AdapterFactory` and configure the Memcached servers. Then assign it to a session manager and start the session:

```php
<?php

use Phalcon\Session\Adapter\Libmemcached;
use Phalcon\Session\Manager;
use Phalcon\Storage\AdapterFactory;
use Phalcon\Storage\SerializerFactory;

$options = [
    'client'  => [],
    'servers' => [
        [
            'host'   => '127.0.0.1',
            'port'   => 11211,
            'weight' => 0,
        ],
    ],
];

$session           = new Manager();
$serializerFactory = new SerializerFactory();
$factory           = new AdapterFactory($serializerFactory);
$memcached         = new Libmemcached($factory, $options);

$session
    ->setAdapter($memcached)
    ->start();
```

The `servers` array can contain multiple Memcached servers, each with `host`, `port`, and `weight` values [1]. This session adapter uses Phalcon’s storage Libmemcached adapter internally and requires the PHP `memcached` extension [1][5]. It uses the session key prefix `sess-memc-` and disables prefix stripping by default [1].

